    "result_text": "All 21 tests across 11 classes pass \u2014 0 failures, 0 errors. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` \u2192 shared `householdId` feature for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**Behavior:** When a request sets `sharesHousehold: true` and another owner already shares the same last name and address (matched case-insensitively, whitespace-collapsed), the new owner is allowed (no 409) and both the new owner and existing household members are stamped with the same stable `householdId`, which is returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`. The id is derived deterministically from the normalized last name + address (`HH-<12 hex>`), so all members of a household converge on the same value.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added read-only `householdId` to the `Owner` schema (generates `OwnerDto.householdId`; mapped automatically by MapStruct, mirroring `customerCode`).\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 new `householdId` field (`household_id` column) with getter/setter.\n- **DB schemas** \u2014 added `household_id` to `owners` in hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres `schema.sql`, plus a trailing `NULL` on the 10 positional seed rows in `db/hsqldb/data.sql` (the tests run on hsqldb; h2/postgres seeds use explicit column lists and were unaffected).\n- **`OwnerHousehold.java`** (new) \u2014 shared helper: `normalize`, `sameHousehold`, and the stable `id(...)` derivation (SHA-256 based).\n- **`CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique.java`** \u2014 refactored to use the shared helper; still throws 409 when `sharesHousehold` is false.\n- **`AssignHousehold.java`** (new) \u2014 after `BuildOwner`, stamps the shared id on the new owner and back-fills existing household members lacking one. If nobody else is in the household, the id is left null.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `assignHousehold` step (under `transaction` governance) between `build` and `assignCustomerCode`.\n\nThe `sharesHousehold` field remains write-only (never returned), per the existing spec.",
